&lt;h3 id="transform-your-server-into-an-ad-blocking-powerhouse-with-pi-hole-and-podman"
>
Transform Your Server into an Ad-Blocking Powerhouse with Pi-hole and Podman!
&lt;/h3>
&lt;a data-clipboard-text="https://chetansource.github.io/posts/home-server-setup-guide-part5/#transform-your-server-into-an-ad-blocking-powerhouse-with-pi-hole-and-podman" class="gblog-post__anchor clip flex align-center" aria-label="Anchor Transform Your Server into an Ad-Blocking Powerhouse with Pi-hole and Podman!" href="#transform-your-server-into-an-ad-blocking-powerhouse-with-pi-hole-and-podman">
&lt;svg class="gblog-icon gblog_link">&lt;use xlink:href="#gblog_link">&lt;/use>&lt;/svg>
&lt;/a>
&lt;/div>
&lt;p>&lt;span style="font-size: 1.2em;">Ready to banish ads and trackers from every device on your network? In this guide, I’ll walk you through setting up &lt;strong>Pi-hole&lt;/strong> a powerful DNS-based ad blocker using &lt;strong>Podman&lt;/strong>, a lightweight, daemonless container engine, on your home server. Say goodbye to intrusive pop-ups and hello to a cleaner, faster browsing experience all while keeping your setup secure and efficient. Let’s dive in!&lt;/span>&lt;/p></description></item><item><title>Home Server Setup Guide (Part 4): Self-Hosting Passwords with Vaultwarden and Tailscale</title><link>https://chetansource.github.io/posts/home-server-setup-guide-part4/</link><pubDate>Thu, 27 Mar 2025 09:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://chetansource.github.io/posts/home-server-setup-guide-part4/</guid><description>&lt;div class="flex align-center gblog-post__anchorwrap">
